xnu-8796's arm64 boot_args carry a 608-byte command line; xnu-10063 (the iPad board) and DarwinBoot use 1024. The loader writes the
1024-byte layout, so on 8796 the kernel kept only the first 607 characters of the fajita iOS 16 command line (the display, HID,
keystore, autoreset and diag-export arguments never arrived) and read bootFlags and memSizeActual from the middle of the
command line. Use the loader's layout.

--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
  * This value matches iBoot's IBOOT_MAX_ENV_VAR_DATA_SIZE.
  * There are no iBoot headers so have to duplicate it here for now.
  */
-#define BOOT_LINE_LENGTH        608
+#define BOOT_LINE_LENGTH        1024
 
